// 486:4
[com_4]
type=text
x=20
y=35
width=40
height=45
widthmode=minus
heightmode=minus
layer=com_2
noclickthrough=yes
textfont=fontmetrics_27
fontmono=no
text=- Hats and Headwear cause the new avatar head to be replaced by the old avatar head<br>- Eyebrow and eyes seem to be misshapen and positioned incorrectly with some walk animations<br>- Torso can be invisible/missing<br>- Feet can be invisible/missing<br>- Gaps and seams between parts of the avatar - such as on the neck or around the waist<br>- Positioning issues where the torso and legs are disconnected<br>- Hair can either be floating away from the head or positioned incorrectly/stretching<br>- Neck position can be incorrect, with the neck being too far forward<br>- Issues where the torso is positioned incorrectly and floats down near the players knees<br>- Hair can clip with the avatar's head<br>- Some hairstyles are currently untextured/look flat<br>- Some hairstyles are stretching when the player moves<br>- Some worn items clip through the head<br>- Some hats and tiaras force the old head model on top of the new one<br>- Facial hair on male characters can result in them being broken, positioned incorrectly<br>- Legs can become misshapen and bend backwards<br>- Worn items and cosmetic overrides that show skin on the avatar will show skin from the old model<br>- Head slot worn items and cosmetics may cause issues with animations/clipping<br>- Appearance of the character within interfaces may not look representative<br>- Textures on hairstyles are not final<br>- Clipping issues can be seen when using freecam.
onload=script20490(event_com, 2100, 1, 0)

